+## Configured BrickLink credential recovery coverage
+
+When api.env enables market access, configuration.tar must also contain exactly
+`<BVA_MARKET_CREDENTIALS_ROOT>/.local/secrets/bricklink.env`. The existing api.env
+member preserves the root/account-scope settings. No credential directory or
+unrelated secret is added. Paired settings, a canonical production root/account
+identity, ordinary paths, private single-link file ownership, API-user traversal
+and the existing local credential parser are required; unsafe or incomplete
+configuration refuses capture rather than claiming market recovery coverage.
+The credential-specific service-owner admission does not relax root-owned checks
+for any other configuration file. Live permissions are not changed.
+
+Receipt schemas 2/3 and the encrypted repositories are unchanged. Historical
+backups remain readable and retain their actual captured coverage; an older
+configuration archive without the credential cannot be described as covering it.
+The credential is included only in a newly verified complete run.
+
+A configuration-only recovery must verify the exact receipt/snapshot bytes,
+reject duplicate, absolute, traversing, link or special archive members, and
+restore only the selected environment and credential files into fresh protected
+disposable storage. Preserve archived file ownership/mode and reconstruct a
+traversable protected root with a private service-owned secrets directory. Verify
+credential equality privately and run the existing loader as the API user under
+its service protections with networking disabled. Never overwrite live settings
+or restore a database for this check. Remove only ownership-verified disposable
+plaintext; retain encrypted snapshots and protected receipts.
